// ===========================================================================
// === region:shell — dispatch ===
// ===========================================================================
const USAGE = `faff — the bundled CLI for the faff skill suite.

Subcommands:
  config <path|get|spec-docs-path|dump|resolved> ...  resolve / read .faffrc (resolved = echo non-default slots)
  config init --set k=v [--set ...] [--force] [--dry-run]   write/merge a tracking block into .faffrc.yaml (--selftest runs the table)
  runcheck [--hook] [--recover] [--json] [--selftest] [RUN_DIR]   audit a /faff-beep-boop run ledger; --hook applies the ownership+liveness gate — silent for a foreign HELD run (FAFF-205, heartbeat-only liveness FAFF-233), and a foreign not-held run only WARNs, never hard-blocks (FAFF-235); only an OWNING session or --recover (deliberate human recovery) hard-blocks; --selftest runs the gate table
  heartbeat [RUN_DIR] [--json]                  FAFF-355: the single sanctioned write path for run liveness — refresh the dedicated .faff/runs/<run-id>/heartbeat file to now on the resolved run (arg → $FAFF_RUN_DIR → latest under .faff/runs), so a live-but-quiet build's long sub-steps (faff-graft gate ladder / review / holdout) keep the run HELD instead of ageing out the staleness window (FAFF-205 liveness, heartbeat-only FAFF-233). The tick's ONLY write is that file (tmp + rename) — it never touches the run ledger, so N concurrent tickers can never clobber an orchestrator outcome write. Every read seam overlays the file over the legacy owner.last_heartbeat ledger field (effective heartbeat = the max of both), so a pre-upgrade run keeps working with zero migration. Soft no-op (exit 0, written:false) when there is no ledger / no owner / owner.status != "running" (a done run is never resurrected, and no file is written); exit 2 on a malformed ledger (loud); --json prints { run_dir, last_heartbeat, written }; --selftest runs the effectiveHeartbeatIso/overlayHeartbeat + held-interaction table
  prepcheck [--hook] [--json] [--root DIR]      FAFF-178: audit faff-prep attach-state markers (.faff/prep/*.json) — block on any produced-but-not-attached spec; --hook blocks at Stop (decision payload, exit 0), plain prints a report + exit 3 if open; --selftest runs the table
  intakecheck <issue> [--labels csv] [--interactive] [--json] [--root DIR]   FAFF-212/223: intake-provenance guard — verify a ticket entered through a sanctioned front door (CLI-written .faff/provenance/<ISSUE>.json marker; the spoofable faff-jot-intake label is a grandfather bridge; a human-set faff-automate is admitted as the eligibility-gesture basis — write-abstained ⇒ human-set by construction, FAFF-218); PURE (no tracker call — labels passed via --labels); exit 0 satisfied · 3 unsatisfied under intake_gate=block ONLY (warn never blocks, off always 0) · 2 usage; --interactive makes a block-mode miss exit 0 with a [warn] (human-at-keyboard is the sanction — autonomous OMITS it); malformed marker → absent + warn, never crash; --selftest runs the bases + bypass table. NOT a Stop-hook (would reintroduce FAFF-205)
  intake-record <issue> --via jot|backfill|fast-track [--reason "<text>"] [--initiated interactive|autonomous] [--json] [--root DIR]   FAFF-212/220: write/update the provenance marker (schema 2) and emit a faff-contract:intake-record descriptor (jot Step 4 calls --via jot). MIGRATION / agent-orchestrator tool — NOT the human steady-state remedy (a human just sets faff-automate in the tracker, FAFF-223): --via backfill is for bulk legacy backfill, --via fast-track REQUIRES --reason (recorded override) or exits 2 writing nothing; --initiated stamps the audit-only initiation mode (invalid → exit 2; absent → key omitted, merge-preserved); --selftest runs the via + initiated tables
  contain <mandate> (--parent <id> | --root) --ancestry <json> [--json]   FAFF-219 (Split A of FAFF-217): subtree-of-mandate containment primitive — answers \`parent ∈ subtree(mandate)\` by walking the AGENT-SUPPLIED parentId chain (--ancestry, a JSON array of {id, parentId}) from <parent> up to <mandate>; reaching the mandate = contained, exhausting to a different root / unknown link / cycle = outward. PURE (no tracker call — parity with eligible/next/intakecheck). exit 0 contained · 3 outward (FAIL-CLOSED: --root, unknown/absent parentId, cycle, or out-of-subtree) · 2 usage/malformed-args. Base case mandate==parent → contained. v1 ISSUE-LEVEL mandates only (sub-issue parentId chain); container/initiative mandates deferred (FAFF-222). --selftest runs the contained/outward/fail-closed table
  budget check [--run-dir DIR] [--until HH:MM] [--max N] [--now-ms MS | --now ISO] [--json]   FAFF-36: run cost / compute budgeting — emit a BudgetState JSON {spent,tokens_source,breached,outcome,warnings?} from the run-ledger + config budget: block + the run's local transcripts. PURE (no tracker/network — parity with next/eligible): tokens summed from the $CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID transcript + child agent-*.jsonl whose own sessionId == this run's (mtime is a cheap pre-filter only, NOT the attribution gate — FAFF-229), baselined at run start; estimate fallback (attempts x est) when the transcript is unavailable, labelled tokens_source=estimate. Dimensions until·max_attempts·tokens·cost (unset = unbounded); at_ceiling stop|narrow|escalate (default stop). --until/--max override config. FAFF-427: budget.cost prices per-model x per-class from a built-in map by DEFAULT (pricing:"map" — no price_per_mtok needed; an unpriced model is priced at the map's costliest known rate, never silently undercounted); an explicit price_per_mtok > 0 keeps the legacy flat-scalar cost byte-for-byte (pricing:"flat", plus a deprecation warning). Cost warnings surface only when budget.cost is actually configured. A malformed budget.until/--until (not valid HH:MM) never becomes a vacuous ceiling that silently never breaches — it degrades to warnings (present only when non-empty, mirrored to stderr) naming the raw value, breached never contains "until" for it, and exit stays 0 (FAFF-364: a non-zero exit here would fail-OPEN the whole budget signal for sentryReadBudget/run-done --budget, which degrade any non-zero child to the unbreached default). --now-ms <epoch-ms> / --now <ISO> is a HERMETIC test/diagnostic-only clock override for the time-based fields (spent.elapsed_ms + the resolved --until wall) — explicit flag only (no ambient/env form), precedence --now-ms > --now > Date.now() (the production default; no production caller passes it); an unparseable injected value exits 2 (never a silent fall-through) (FAFF-302). breached != {} is the terminating signal. FAFF-425: the run's OWN ledger being unreadable (explicitly-named and absent, or present-but-corrupt) is a distinct own-fault — never coerced into an all-clear reading — emitting {outcome:"indeterminate",indeterminate:true,reason} and exiting 3; a legitimately empty surface (no run requested, none found) is unaffected, unchanged outcome:"none" at exit 0. --selftest runs the table
  economics [--run-dir DIR] [--by class|model|mcp|day|effort] [--json]   FAFF-357: per-run unit economics — emit a UnitEconomics JSON {run_id,tokens_total,tokens_source,price_per_mtok,pricing,cost_total,buckets,shipped_count,attempt_count,cost_per_shipped,cost_per_attempt,per_issue,zero_ship,warnings} deriving cost-per-shipped-issue + cost-per-attempt from the run-ledger outcomes + budget check's transcript-summed this-run tokens. PURE, RENDERING-ONLY (no tracker/network/LLM — parity with budget check/runcheck): reuses budget's exact token path (measureTokens baselined at run start; estimate fallback labelled tokens_source=estimate) and DOES NOT touch any producer (ledger/budget/events unchanged). FAFF-427: the top-line prices via the SAME map + rate source budget.cost uses — pricing:"map" by DEFAULT (no price_per_mtok needed); cost_total is THIS RUN's per-model spend (baselined at run start, consistent with tokens_total + budget check's spent.cost), so the "two cost figures" gap (a rate difference, not a population one) is closed — at a run-start baseline of 0 it equals the sum of --by model's priced rows; an explicit price_per_mtok > 0 keeps pricing:"flat", the legacy flat-scalar top-line byte-for-byte; an unpriced model's tokens are excluded from cost_total (reported cost:null for that row, named in warnings) while priced models still sum. cost_* null + no dollar column when nothing could be priced; zero_ship (0 shipped, >0 tokens) flagged loud; attempt_count excludes routed-out/unreached-budget; per_issue is best-effort meta.json attribution (session-owned agent-*.jsonl, [A-Z]+-\d+ in description matched to a ledger outcome), run-level figures never depend on it. beep-boop's Reporting step renders the block. FAFF-410: --by class|model|mcp|day pivots the SAME transcript walk into per-class/per-model/per-day/per-MCP-tool buckets priced per-model×per-class (built-in PRICE_PER_MTOK + optional budget.price_per_mtok_by_model override; unknown model→cost:null); class/model/day reconcile to the top-line total, --by mcp reuses FAFF-409's MEASURED per-tool cache-read attribution; --by X --json rides a breakdown object, --by X (no --json) prints a skimmable table, NO --by is byte-for-byte unchanged; unknown axis exits 2 naming {class,model,mcp,day,effort}; non-leak (sizes/counts/names/model-ids/costs only). FAFF-415: --by effort reads the run's events.jsonl (not the transcript — reasoning-effort is a request-time setting the transcript never records), buckets dispatches by their data.effort tag, prices at the run's dominant model (ESTIMATE — events carry no model) and reports coverage_pct vs the top-line. --selftest runs the table
  quality [--run-dir DIR] [--json]   FAFF-418: per-run QUALITY/outcome telemetry — the quality mirror of economics. Emit a QualityReport JSON {run_id,outcomes,shipped_count,attempt_count,parked_count,park_rate,rework{total_turns,reworked_attempts,tagged_attempts,rework_rate,mean_turns},gate_catch,per_issue,source,warnings} from the run-ledger terminal outcomes (authoritative) + the events.jsonl issue-outcome events' FAFF-418 gate/rework tags. PURE, read-only (no tracker/network/LLM — parity with economics/budget check/runcheck). Pairs with economics by SHARING run_id + the exact shipped/attempt denominators (ECONOMICS_BUCKET_ORDER + routed-out/unreached-budget exclusion), so $/quality = economics.cost_per_shipped beside quality.park_rate on one run; no cost duplicated into quality. park_rate/rework_rate are over attempt_count (dispatched builds), null on a zero-attempt run (never 0/0); mean_turns is over tagged_attempts, and a warning flags rework_rate as a lower bound when tags don't cover every attempt; gate_catch is the distribution of which quality gate {structural,adversarial,holdout,ci} caught a non-shipped build; source=ledger+events (or ledger, gate/rework null, when no events.jsonl). --json emits the report, no flag prints a skimmable table; missing run dir exits 2; non-leak (outcome/gate-names/counts/rates only). --selftest runs the pure-core table
  reconcile --run-dir DIR --level L1|L2|L3|L4 [--json] [--selftest]   FAFF-397: the blocking run-end GROUND-TRUTH gate — confronts each ledger \`shipped\` outcome (+ each spec-referenced non-admitted sibling's terminal-state) with LIVE git/forge/tracker evidence the orchestrator gathered (never re-observed here — the verb stays PURE, mirroring merge-gate's decideFloor split; \`runcheck\` audits ledger COMPLETENESS, this audits ledger-vs-WORLD ground-truth, deliberately kept separate so runcheck's no-I/O Stop-hook purity, FAFF-205/233/235, is never touched). Reads a ReconcileInput {level,shipped[],siblings[]} on stdin, emits a faff-contract:run-reconcile block {divergences,consistent,disposition}. Divergence classes: phantom-merge (shipped's recorded merge-record.json head_sha != the observed merged head_sha) / claimed-shipped-unmerged (no merge-record, or observed pr_merged:false — fail-closed: unprovable ⇒ divergence) / unowned-sibling-mutation (a non-admitted, spec-referenced sibling flipped INTO a terminal state during the run). disposition is level-gated: consistent → pass; a divergence → needs-human at L4 (hard-block/escalate — the only level nothing is watching), warn at ≤L3 (surfaced, non-blocking). exit 0 consistent / 1 divergence(s) / 2 malformed ReconcileInput or missing --run-dir/--level (fail-loud, never a silent pass); --selftest runs the divergence-class + level-gating + validate table
  run-done [--queue-empty] [--all-parked] [--ledger-clean] [--budget JSON] [--prd-coverage JSON | --no-prd] [--inflection reached|none] [--non-convergence] [--policy JSON] [--json]   FAFF-38: the terminating-condition predicate — compose faff's shipped run signals into the one decision that ends a /faff-beep-boop run (run-complete | continue | escalate). PURE (no tracker/network/disk beyond args; NEVER calls the methodology — the orchestrator resolves the policy and passes --policy). Reimplements no signal: reads queue state + runcheck's .clean (--ledger-clean) + budget check's {breached,outcome} (--budget) + prdr coverage's prd-satisfied (--prd-coverage → .satisfied; --no-prd for no PRD in scope). FIXED safety floor (no --policy may weaken it): budget-escalate → escalate · unclean ledger at drain → continue/undispatched-ledger · prd_satisfied==false → escalate/product-incomplete. POLICY-WEIGHTED rungs (the structural-default ladder, overridable by the methodology's run-termination-policy via --policy): non-convergence→escalate · budget-narrow→continue · budget-stop→complete · value-inflection→complete · work-remaining→continue · drained|all-parked→complete. Emits a RunDoneVerdict {verdict,reason,signals,policy_source,conformant,violations}, schemaCheck'd against run-termination belt-and-braces; malformed JSON → exit 2; report-only exit 0 (the verdict is in the payload). --selftest runs the table
  hooks-ensure [--root DIR] [--json] [--dry-run]   FAFF-192/200/434: idempotently register faff's Stop-hook command set (runcheck + prepcheck --hook) AND the PreToolUse merge-fence (merge-fence --hook) in .claude/settings.json, AND normalize a present hook whose command path diverged from the canonical form — non-destructive, byte-stable no-op when present+canonical, skips a subcommand the resolved faff can't serve; exit 2 on malformed settings; --selftest runs the table
  merge-fence --hook [--root DIR] [--selftest]   FAFF-434: the outermost mechanical wall against a raw gh pr merge Bash call — a PreToolUse hook (registered by hooks-ensure) shaped like runcheck/prepcheck's --hook/--selftest split. --hook reads a PreToolUse JSON event on stdin ({tool_name, tool_input:{command}}); a match on the pure matcher matchesRawGhMerge (a gh token — path/env-prefix tolerant — followed by pr then merge, any whitespace between) writes a single deny line to stderr naming faff merge-gate as the sanctioned remedy and exits 2; anything else — non-Bash tool, absent/non-string command, malformed/empty stdin — exits 0 silently, never blocking. faff merge-gate's own merge is a spawnSync child process, not a Bash tool call, so it is invisible to this fence by construction (no allowlist needed). --root DIR is accepted-and-ignored (present only so hooks-ensure's probeServes, which always passes it, never misclassifies a serving bin as unserved); --selftest drives the pure matcher + event-decision tables
  validate-adapters [--skills-dir DIR]          lint shipped slot-skill conformance
  validate-adapters --configured [--root DIR]   pre-flight a user's configured (swapped-in) slot occupants
  labels [--names]                              print the canonical faff control-label manifest (JSON; --names for bare names)
  label add|remove <issue-id> <label> [--present-label L ...]   FAFF-187: emit a faff-contract:label-op descriptor (issue·label·action·ensure-first·idempotent-noop) for a control-label mutation the agent performs via MCP — PURE, no tracker I/O; rejects a label not in the manifest; --present-label (repeatable) pre-computes the idempotent no-op; --selftest runs the table
  eligible --label L [--label L ...] [--default opt-in|opt-out]   FAFF-61: is a ticket automation-eligible? (true/false; hold>automate>default); --selftest runs the table
  spec-review-lenses --tags T,T,... --level L1|L2|L3|L4 --appetite low|medium|high|full [--selftest]   FAFF-268: cost-gate IN FRONT of the spec_review producer — maps a spec's CLASSIFIED change-surface tags + level + appetite to a LensSelection {lenses,mode,rationale}. Pure; the signal->tag classification is prose-side (faff-prep). v1 additive-only/safe-direction: only architectural (or methodology when no tag adds it) is dropped; infosec+QA sticky at L1-L3; unclassified/unknown tag -> all four (fail-safe); L4 -> adversarial all-four (never narrowed); low/medium appetite widens to all four. --selftest runs the table
  dod classify --spec <path|-> [--json]         FAFF-34: classify a spec's DoD criteria (## Scenarios + ### N. DONE) by born-verifiability class (scenario|assertion|prose), reusing classifyCriterion verbatim — the evaluator uses this to decide which criteria it may machine-judge vs force to needs-human (prose). PURE (file/stdin in, JSON out, no tracker/network/LLM); emits {criteria:[{text,class,source}],counts}; exit 0 on a successful parse / 2 usage/unreadable; --selftest runs the table
  holdout verdict --issue <id> [--dir .faff/holdout] [--json]   FAFF-311: the per-issue merge-floor GATE lookup for faff-graft Step 10 (Decision 4 → Option A). Reads the single .faff/holdout/<id>.json, re-validates it through the SAME computeHoldoutVerdict gate (via holdoutGateResult, never a forked rule), and reduces it to pass|block keyed to the issue being built, BEFORE the FAFF-277 PRDR fold. Fail-closed: a missing/unreadable/malformed/non-blind/incoherent verdict or any aggregate != meets-spec is block (exit 1); a conformant code_blind:true meets-spec is pass (exit 0); missing --issue is exit 2. Emits {issue,gate,reason,aggregate?,code_blind?,violations?}; a block also summarised to stderr. PURE beyond the single-file read (no tracker/network/LLM). The same file still feeds 'faff holdout verdicts --association' unchanged (one artifact, two consumers)
  holdout verdicts --association <json|@file|-> [--dir .faff/holdout] [--json]   FAFF-277: pure, trust-gated bridge from the evaluator's persisted holdout verdicts (.faff/holdout/<issue|run>.json) to the already-shipped 'faff prdr coverage --dod-verdicts' flag. Reads each verdict, RE-VALIDATES it through the same computeHoldoutVerdict gate (never a forked rule), translates only a conformant code_blind:true meets-spec -> the literal "met", folds conservatively per PRDR (any non-met sibling makes the PRDR not-met), and keys by the supplied issue->PRDR association; every other aggregate passes through (!= met), untrusted files are omitted. Emits {verdicts:{prdr:value},skipped:[{key,reason}]}; skipped also summarised to stderr. PURE (filesystem read of --dir only, no tracker/network/LLM). Absent --dir -> empty map (exit 0); missing/non-object --association, malformed --association JSON, or unreadable --dir -> exit 2; a successful run (incl. empty map) -> exit 0 (no exit 1, report-only). --selftest runs the table
  admissible --spec <path|-> [--lights-out] [--json]   FAFF-224: lights-out quality-IN gate — pure structural check over a spec's machine-verifiable DoD (## Scenarios + ### N. DONE). Gating R1 (>=1 born-verifiable scenario) / R2a (non-empty DONE) / R2b (no banned-vague DONE item); advisory R3 (runnable-check command -> warnings, never gates) / advisory R4 (FAFF-306: SCENARIOS and DONE headings at different levels -> warnings, never gates — the historical over-capture smell). NO LLM, never re-invokes the producer; reads spec via file or stdin, zero tracker/network. Fail-safe: ambiguous/unparseable/absent DoD -> inadmissible; --lights-out absent -> admissible no-op (L1-L3 unchanged). Emits AdmissibilityVerdict {admissible,reasons,checks,warnings}; exit 0 admissible / 1 inadmissible / 2 usage; --selftest runs the verdict table
