  engine call --lane methodology|intake --system FILE --user FILE [--root DIR]   FAFF-422: one-shot local-engine dispatch for an engine-valued pure-data-in lane — resolve models.<lane> = engine:<name> against the top-level engines: map (provider/model/host/api_key_env; provider families ollama | openai-compatible aliases, anthropic REFUSED — that's what the Agent-token vocabulary is for), family-conditional preflight (ollama /api/tags, openai /v1/models — engine-unreachable vs model-not-served are distinct named exits), then ONE non-streaming completion (ollama /api/chat stream:false; openai /v1/chat/completions); stdout is the completion text (the producer output). FAIL-LOUD, terminal, no retry/fallback chain — the caller NEVER re-dispatches on the session model. The lane allowlist (methodology | intake) is enforced at dispatch here AND at config read (validateModelLane); a non-inherit effort.<lane> on an engine-valued lane is refused (a knob that silently does nothing is forbidden). exit 0 ok · 2 usage/config fault (non-allowlisted lane, unknown engine, missing field, anthropic provider, effort conflict) · 4 model-not-served · 5 engine-unreachable · 6 auth-failed (declared api_key_env unset, or HTTP 401/403) · 7 malformed-response; --selftest runs the request/parse/preflight/orchestration table (no network)
  models build-for <confidence> [--root DIR]     FAFF-334: per-issue build-model routing. Print the build model Agent-token for an issue of the given retained spec confidence (high|medium|…), via the OPTIONAL sibling matcher \`models.build_by_confidence\` (a default + confidence-keyed leaves) that extends FAFF-315's per-run \`models.build\` scalar. PURE (confidence passed in, no tracker call). Fallback: build_by_confidence.<conf> → .default → models.build (scalar) → inherit; the resolved token is validated against the closed build set (exit 2 fail-loud, never a silent inherit); an absent/unknown confidence routes to the default bucket. Matcher absent ⇒ the scalar path, byte-for-byte FAFF-315. "inherit" ⇒ caller omits the Agent-tool model param; --selftest runs the resolver + matcher-leaf-validation table
  regions <list|check|selftest> [--json] [--region governance|factory|all]   FAFF-359: the logical governance/factory boundary (ADR 0042). list prints the single in-code region map (command → region; --json for the object). check is the direction lint over THIS file's region-tagged section banners — a governance span referencing a factory identifier, or a shared-infra span referencing either region's, is a violation naming both ends (comment/string/regex-literal mentions ignored; template interpolations still count); exit 0 clean / 1 violation(s) / 2 malformed (untagged banner, unknown region, cross-region duplicate top-level name, or REGION_MAP/COMMANDS drift); no suppression mechanism. selftest spawns each member command's own --selftest per the explicit REGION_SELFTEST_ARGV allowlist (default --region all) and prints a per-command pass/fail table — a governance member without a selftest is FATAL, a factory one is reported no-selftest; exit 2 before any spawn on allowlist drift (unlisted command, or a stale no-selftest entry); --selftest runs the lint fixture table
`;


// ===========================================================================
// === region:shell — subcommand registry + main dispatch ===
// ===========================================================================
// Subcommand registry (ADR 0014) — the single source of truth for the CLI command
// set. main() dispatches through this map, and `Object.keys(COMMANDS)` is exactly
// the canonical set `lint-cli-doc` asserts docs/guide/cli.md documents. Adding a
// subcommand = one entry here (and a docs/guide/cli.md row, or lint-cli-doc fails CI).
// The -h/--help/help aliases are handled in main() and are deliberately NOT entries.
// ===========================================================================
const COMMANDS = {
  "config": cmdConfig,
  "sync": cmdSync,
  "runcheck": cmdRuncheck,
  "heartbeat": cmdHeartbeat,
  "prepcheck": cmdPrepcheck,
  "intakecheck": cmdIntakecheck,
  "intake-record": cmdIntakeRecord,
  "contain": cmdContain,
  "budget": cmdBudget,
  "economics": cmdEconomics,
  "quality": cmdQuality,
  "reconcile": cmdReconcile,
  "run-done": cmdRunDone,
  "hooks-ensure": cmdHooksEnsure,
  "merge-fence": cmdMergeFence,
  "validate-adapters": cmdValidateAdapters,
  "labels": cmdLabels,
  "label": cmdLabel,
  "eligible": cmdEligible,
  "admissible": cmdAdmissible,
  "dod": cmdDod,
  "holdout": cmdHoldout,
  "spec-review-lenses": cmdSpecReviewLenses,
  "container-check": cmdContainerCheck,
  "corrective-integrity": cmdCorrectiveIntegrity,
  "merge-gate": cmdMergeGate,
  "branch-protection-check": cmdBranchProtectionCheck,
  "next": cmdNext,
  "project-next": cmdProjectNext,
  "state": cmdState,
  "park-history": cmdParkHistory,
  "gitignore-ensure": cmdGitignoreEnsure,
  "adr": cmdAdr,
  "prd": cmdPrd,
  "prdr": cmdPrdr,
  "profile": cmdProfile,
  "fixtures": cmdFixtures,
  "env": cmdEnv,
  "engine": cmdEngine,
  "events": cmdEvents,
  "effects": cmdEffects,
  "review-progress": cmdReviewProgress,
  "build-progress": cmdBuildProgress,
  "sentry": cmdSentry,
  "lights-out": cmdLightsOut,
  "audit": cmdAudit,
  "gates": cmdGates,
  "contract": cmdContract,
  "doctor": cmdDoctor,
  "worktree-prune": cmdWorktreePrune,
  "worktree-root": cmdWorktreeRoot,
  "lint-refs": cmdLintRefs,
  "lint-cli-doc": (args) => cmdLintCliDoc(args, COMMANDS),
  "regions": (args) => cmdRegions(args, COMMANDS),
  "models": cmdModels,
};

function main(argv) {
  const [sub, ...rest] = argv;
  if (!sub) { process.stderr.write(USAGE); return 2; }
  if (sub === "-h" || sub === "--help" || sub === "help") { process.stdout.write(USAGE); return 0; }
  const handler = COMMANDS[sub];
  if (handler) return handler(rest);
  process.stderr.write(`faff: unknown subcommand '${sub}'\n\n${USAGE}`);
  return 2;
}

// Run as a CLI only when invoked directly (shebang / `node …/bin/faff <sub>`), so a
// `require`/ESM `import` of this file for its exported pure functions (the FAFF-373
// corrective-integrity tests) does NOT execute a subcommand.
if (require.main === module) {
  // FAFF-422: `engine call` is the first async handler (network one-shot) — a returned
  // Promise resolves to the exit code; every other handler stays a plain synchronous int.
  // The rejection arm is belt-and-braces: cmdEngine maps every internal error to an exit
  // code, so the promise resolves in practice — but an unforeseen reject (e.g. an EPIPE
  // from a broken stdout pipe) must still fail loud with a non-zero exit, never a silent 0.
  const r = main(process.argv.slice(2));
  if (r && typeof r.then === "function") {
    r.then((code) => { process.exitCode = code; },
           (e) => { process.stderr.write(`faff: unhandled error — ${(e && e.message) || e}\n`); process.exitCode = 2; });
  } else process.exitCode = r;
}

// Exported pure functions (FAFF-373). Extensionless CJS imported from ESM exposes

// Exported pure functions (FAFF-373). Extensionless CJS imported from ESM exposes
// only the default export, so tests destructure this object.
module.exports = { correctiveIntegrityProbe, integrityGate, correctiveIntegrityDirs };
